.TH TODO 1 "September 2026" "todo-cli 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
todo \- terminal todo list manager with weather and news
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B todo
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B todo
is a command line todo list manager.  Tasks are stored in a local SQLite
database.  It also provides weather lookup (via wttr.in) and news reading
(via configurable RSS/Atom feeds), implemented as Python helper scripts
invoked through a pipe by the C core.
.PP
Supported platforms: Linux, macOS, and Windows.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "project add " name
Create a project. Names are case-sensitive and may contain UTF-8 text.
Quote names containing spaces. Duplicate or empty names are rejected.
.TP
.B project [list]
List projects with pending, completed and total task counts.
.TP
.BI "project show " name
Show pending tasks grouped under P0, P1, P2 and P3, followed by Completed
and Progress: completed/total. Task IDs are shown next to titles.
.TP
.BR add " \fIproject title...\fR [\-p \fIP0|P1|P2|P3\fR] [\-d \fIYYYY\-MM\-DD\fR]"
Add a task to an existing project. Priority is P0 (highest) through P3
(lowest), default P2. The long option is
.BR \-\-priority .
Numeric values 0/1/2/3 are also accepted.
With only one title argument, the default project is TODO.
Use an explicit
.BI \-\-project " name"
to treat all positional arguments as title words.
The due date must have the form YYYY\-MM\-DD. Everything after a lone
.B \-\-
is treated literally; if it precedes all title words, the default project is TODO.
.TP
.BR list " | " ls " [project] [\-\-project name] [\-p|\-\-priority P0|P1|P2|P3]"
List tasks. Project, priority and status filters can be combined.
By default only pending tasks across all projects are shown. Use
.B \-\-all
to show everything or
.B \-\-done
to show completed tasks only. These status flags are mutually exclusive
with each other and with
.BR \-\-todo .
.B \-\-pending
is an alias for
.BR \-\-todo .
.TP
.BI "done " id...
Mark tasks as completed. IDs are unique across all projects.
.TP
.BI "undo " id...
Revert tasks to pending.
.TP
.BR delete " | " del " | " rm " \fIid...\fR"
Delete tasks.
.TP
.BI "edit " id " " new\-title...
Change the title of a task.
.TP
.B clear
Delete all completed tasks.
.TP
.B stats
Print task counts: total, completed, and pending.
.TP
.BI "weather " [city]
Show current weather.  Without a city the location is detected from the
IP address; otherwise the configured default city is used.
.TP
.BI "news " [feed1,feed2,...]
Show the latest headlines from RSS/Atom feeds.  Without arguments the
configured feed list is used.
.TP
.B version
Print version information.
.TP
.BR \-\-help " | " \-h " | " help
Print full help.
.PP
All subcommands also accept
.BR \-\-help .
Help and version queries do not open the database.
.SH UPGRADING
Version 0.1 databases are migrated automatically in a transaction.
Existing tasks are assigned to the TODO project; IDs, timestamps,
completion status and due dates are preserved. Old numeric priorities
1/2/3 become P1/P2/P3. Failed migrations are rolled back.
Databases with a newer schema version are rejected without modification.
Use version 0.2 or later after migration.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I data_dir/todo.db
SQLite database.  On Linux/macOS the default
.I data_dir
is
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/todo-cli
(or
.IR ~/.local/share/todo-cli );
on Windows it is
.IR %APPDATA%\\todo-cli .
.TP
.I config_dir/todo-cli/config.ini
Optional configuration file, INI style with
.I key = value
lines and
.B #
or
.B ;
comments.  On Linux/macOS the default
.I config_dir
is
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
(or
.IR ~/.config );
on Windows it is
.IR %APPDATA% .
See
.B CONFIGURATION
below.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B data_dir
Directory where
.I todo.db
is stored.
.TP
.B python
Python interpreter (a single executable name or path).
Defaults to
.B python3
on Unix and
.B python
on Windows.
.TP
.B script_dir
Directory containing
.I weather.py
and
.IR news.py .
Detected automatically; override only if needed.
.TP
.B default_city
Default city for the weather command.  Empty means IP-based location.
.TP
.B news_feeds
Comma-separated list of RSS/Atom feed URLs.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TODO_CLI_DATA_DIR
Overrides
.BR data_dir .
.TP
.B TODO_CLI_PYTHON
Overrides
.BR python .
.TP
.B TODO_CLI_SCRIPT_DIR
Overrides
.BR script_dir .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error (database, network, or script failure).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (unknown command or invalid arguments).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Create a project, add a P0 task and display its progress:
.RS
.nf
todo project add NanoX
todo add NanoX "Fix crash" \-\-priority P0
todo project show NanoX
todo list NanoX \-\-priority P0 \-\-todo
todo project list
.fi
.RE
.PP
Add, list, complete and delete a task:
.RS
.nf
todo add "Review linear equations"
todo list
todo done 1
todo delete 1
todo \-\-help
.fi
.RE
.PP
Add a high-priority task due on a specific date:
.RS
.nf
todo add "Write weekly report" \-p 1 \-d 2026\-10\-01
.fi
.RE
.PP
List all tasks, complete tasks 1 and 3, then check the stats:
.RS
.nf
todo list \-\-all
todo done 1 3
todo stats
.fi
.RE
.PP
Query the weather in Beijing and read the configured news feeds:
.RS
.nf
todo weather Beijing
todo news
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sqlite3 (1),
.BR python3 (1)
.PP
Full architecture documentation is provided with the distribution in
.I docs/DESIGN.md
and a sample configuration in
.IR docs/config.ini.example .
